Focused organisation chart with key actors
The next visual places the key actors into a focused TenantThread organisation chart. The full organisation chart is too dense for the main report, so this view keeps John Windward, the relevant actors, and their direct organisational context.

GraphCode Chunk











highlight_people &lt;- c(
  "person:john_windward", "person:chloe_ballast", "person:daniel_gangway",
  "person:gabriel_sonar", "person:mia_fender", "person:lily_anchorline",
  "person:zoey_drydock", "person:victoria_rigging", "person:james_stern"
)

# The full organisation chart is too large for the main report. This focused
# view keeps only the key actors and their direct organisational context.
direct_parent_edges &lt;- org_edges |&gt;
  filter(target %in% highlight_people)

parent_nodes &lt;- unique(direct_parent_edges$source)

grandparent_edges &lt;- org_edges |&gt;
  filter(target %in% parent_nodes)

focused_org_nodes &lt;- unique(c(
  highlight_people,
  direct_parent_edges$source,
  grandparent_edges$source
))

focused_org_edges &lt;- org_edges |&gt;
  filter(source %in% focused_org_nodes, target %in% focused_org_nodes)

org_vis_nodes &lt;- org_nodes |&gt;
  filter(id %in% focused_org_nodes) |&gt;
  mutate(
    group = type,
    color = case_when(
      id == "person:john_windward" ~ "#f4a6a6",
      id %in% highlight_people ~ "#ffe8a3",
      type == "department" ~ "#d9e8fb",
      type == "team" ~ "#eeeeee",
      TRUE ~ "#f8f8f8"
    ),
    size = case_when(
      id == "person:john_windward" ~ 32,
      id %in% highlight_people ~ 24,
      type == "department" ~ 30,
      type == "team" ~ 26,
      TRUE ~ 20
    ),
    title = paste0(
      "&lt;b&gt;", label, "&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;",
      "Type: ", type,
      if_else(!is.na(title), paste0("&lt;br&gt;Title: ", title), "")
    )
  ) |&gt;
  select(id, label, group, color, size, title)

org_vis_edges &lt;- focused_org_edges |&gt;
  transmute(from = source, to = target, label = relation, arrows = "to")

visNetwork(org_vis_nodes, org_vis_edges, height = "620px") |&gt;
  visOptions(highlightNearest = TRUE, nodesIdSelection = TRUE) |&gt;
  visHierarchicalLayout(direction = "UD", sortMethod = "directed", levelSeparation = 120) |&gt;
  visNodes(font = list(size = 16)) |&gt;
  visEdges(font = list(size = 11, align = "middle")) |&gt;
  visPhysics(enabled = FALSE)




Insights.

John Windward appears as the Customer Support department lead. This matters because the post carries more organisational credibility than a random employee account.
Chloe Ballast is also important because the final SwiftWren delegation came from her personal agent to John Windward’s personal agent.
By reducing the full chart to the directly relevant people, teams, and departments, the visual makes the organisational context easier to interpret.
